From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 13:18:41 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] kboot: T6050: report the firmware release to the GPU driver

The Linux G17 driver takes apple,firmware-version of the GPU node as the
hint for which pinned firmware build to measure first. The T6050 hand-off
did not set it, so the driver walked its table in order and logged every
earlier build as an error before it reached the loaded one. On the K116s
(27.2) that is, on every boot:

  aurora 2300000000.gpu: unsupported GPU firmware build: TEXT 0xa4000 ...
  aurora 2300000000.gpu: supported: 26C5035r for T6050 G17S, primary then secondary
  aurora 2300000000.gpu: GPU firmware image not admitted: EINVAL
  aurora 2300000000.gpu: GPU firmware build: 26B8125 for T6050 G17S, primary then secondary

Set the property from the OS firmware version once the hand-off is
published. A failure only loses the hint.

Signed-off-by: Jens Axboe <axboe@kernel.dk>
(cherry picked from commit 5d2ec8f00e996f7e9351f398945b844ba0fb813e)
---
 src/kboot_gpu.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/kboot_gpu.c b/src/kboot_gpu.c
index d44fcddc..daff6683 100644
--- a/src/kboot_gpu.c
+++ b/src/kboot_gpu.c
@@ -4217,6 +4217,13 @@ static T6050_GPU_INIT int dt_set_gpu_t6050(void *dt)
     }
     printf("FDT: GPU: T6050 G17S %s enabled, fw-text at %#lx\n", t6050_gpu.build[step - 2].name,
            r[8]);
+    /*
+     * The driver tries the build of the reported release first. Without the hint it walks its
+     * table in order and logs each earlier build as not admitted before it finds this one.
+     */
+    int gpu = kboot_fdt_path_exact(dt, "gpu");
+    if (gpu < 0 || firmware_set_fdt(dt, gpu, "apple,firmware-version", &os_firmware))
+        printf("FDT: GPU: T6050: no apple,firmware-version for the driver\n");
     if (t6050_gpu_leakage(dt))
         printf("FDT: GPU: no leakage calibration words; the driver's generic configuration\n");
     return 0;
